  "body": "## What changed\n\nA touch probe is never spun (#523). Haas, Tormach, Sinumerik, Heidenhain and Mazak posted `S<rpm> M3` (Mazak `MOTON S…`) for every section, a probe's S0 included. Each now gates its spindle start on `sRpm > 0`, the rule `fanuc.cps` has used since #108. Heidenhain also drops the `S` word from its `TOOL CALL` at rpm 0.\n\n- No extra `M5` is needed: every post already ends each section with `M5`, so a probe section never inherits a running spindle.\n- A cutter can never lose its spindle through this: `Tool::is_sane` refuses rpm 0 on every tool, so S0 reaches a post only from a probe dump.\n- **Reachability:** on main, only Fanuc posts probe moves, and it was already gated. PR #500 (Tormach probe positioning, now merged) made the Tormach path reachable, which is where `S0 M3` showed up in the Hub run; this PR regenerates #500's `golden/nc/tormach/probe_guard_moves.nc`, whose only diff is that dropped `S0 M3` line.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/probe_spindle.rs`:\n- `a_section_with_no_spindle_speed_starts_no_spindle_on_any_mill_post`: an rpm-0 section through all six mill posts posts no `S` word and no `M3`/`M03`/`MOTON`. It fails without the post changes (`haas: a probe section posts [\"S0\", \"M3\"]`).\n- `a_cutting_section_still_starts_its_spindle_on_every_mill_post`: an 8000 rpm section still posts its `S` word and spindle start on all six.\n\n`scripts/gate.sh quick`, which escalated to batch, ran 782 s. Results:\n- geometry, cl, tools, post, sim and motion: green.\n- app: green, 1433 passed and 0 failed across all binaries, conformance and every NC golden byte-exact.\n- clippy `-D warnings` on all 8 crates: green.\n- ui: the only red is the five known failures that are also red on main: the three headless tests that need a GPU adapter, and `structural::shell_structure_dark/light` (the `v0.0.0` label).\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo Hub run of the fixed output. Cutting output is byte-identical (every cutting golden is unchanged); the one golden that moves is #500's Tormach probe program, minus its `S0 M3`.\n\nChangelog: A probing section no longer starts the spindle (S0 M3) on the Haas, Tormach, Siemens, Heidenhain and Mazak posts (#523)\n\nFixes #523\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
